Bootstrap: docker
From: python:3.13-slim

%files
    ./config.py /Test_Predictor/config.py
    ./deBoerTest_model.py /Test_Predictor/deBoerTest_model.py
    ./error_checking_functions.py /Test_Predictor/error_checking_functions.py
    ./predictor_content_handler.py /Test_Predictor/predictor_content_handler.py
    ./predictor_help_message.json /Test_Predictor/predictor_help_message.json
    ./predictor_RestAPI.py /Test_Predictor/predictor_RestAPI.py
    ./schema_validation.py /Test_Predictor/schema_validation.py

%environment
    export APPTAINER_NO_MOUNT="home,tmp,proc,sys,dev"
    export LC_ALL=C

%post
    # Install system packages needed for conda and building extensions
    echo "Installing system dependencies..."
    apt-get update && \
    apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends ca-certificates && \
    apt-get clean && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

    echo "Installing Python dependencies..."
    python3 -m pip install --upgrade pip
    pip3 install --no-cache-dir numpy pandas tqdm msgpack flask

    echo "Removing any __pycache__ directories that snuck in..."
    find /Test_Predictor -type d -name __pycache__ -exec rm -rf {} + 2>/dev/null || true

    echo "Setting permissions..."
    chmod -R 755 /Test_Predictor

%runscript
    exec python3 /Test_Predictor/predictor_RestAPI.py "$@"

%startscript
    exec python3 /Test_Predictor/predictor_RestAPI.py "$@"

%labels
    Authors "Satyam Priyadarshi, Ishika Luthra"


%help
    This container for the Test Predictor includes:
    - A Flask-based REST API (`predictor_RestAPI.py`)
    - The `deBoerTest_model` dummy model, integrated into the predictor, which returns
      randomized predictions for any request type (point, track, interaction_matrix)
    - Request validation and preprocessing (`schema_validation.py`, `error_checking_functions.py`)
    - Content negotiation and (de)serialization for JSON and MessagePack (`predictor_content_handler.py`)
    - Predictor identity and wire-format configuration (`config.py`)
    - Predictor metadata served at `/help` (`predictor_help_message.json`).

    Run the container
    ```
    apptainer run --containall predictor.sif HOST PORT
    ```

    Details:
    - The container launches a Flask-based server to receive data via HTTP POST requests.
    - Replace `HOST` and `PORT` with the server and port configuration for the Evaluator to connect to.

    API Endpoints:
    - `/formats` - GET:  supported request and response formats
    - `/help`    - GET:  predictor metadata and usage information
    - `/predict` - POST: main endpoint for submitting prediction requests

    Purpose:
    - Provides a lightweight, model-free Predictor to test and validate new Evaluators
      against the GAME Predictor API without needing a real trained model.
    - Facilitates end-to-end checks of the request -> predict -> response -> metrics pipeline.

    Example Command:
    ```
    apptainer run --containall predictor.sif 172.xx.xx.xxx 5000
    ```

    Arguments:
    1. `HOST IP`: IP address or hostname of the Predictor server.
    2. `PORT`   : Port number the Predictor is listening on.
